  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR splits the longest release-tier test of issue 1715 into smaller tests. Only test code and one decision file change. No `src/` file changes.\n\n- The heavy test `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_the_3d_finish` is removed from `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies.rs`.\n- The new binary `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies_finish.rs` has six heavy tests in its place. Each test sets the S1 top and bottom heights to one sixth of the model's Z span (118.2 mm). The offsets are from `top_of_model`, and the last band ends on `bottom_of_model`. Each test generates S1 alone and runs `verify`.\n- Each band test keeps the asserts of the old test without change: one generated row, status `ok`, and no `gouge` entry in `gate.problems`.\n- The new default-suite test `the_3d_finish_bands_tile_the_whole_span` asserts that the bands start at the model top, end at the model bottom, and have no gap.\n- `docs/decisions/1715-split-shared-face-bodies.md` records the decision: what a band program proves, and what it does not prove (the links between bands, and level Z values that move by less than one stepdown at a band boundary).\n\nThe release-gate plan (`cargo xtask gate release --dry-run`) has the new step `app heavy: shared_face_bodies_finish`. `shared_face_bodies.rs` has no ignored test now, so the planner gives it no heavy step. The Gate map of the new file names the same modules as the old file.\n\n## `#[test]` count\n\n| File | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies.rs` | 6 (1 ignored) | 5 (0 ignored) |\n| `crates/app/tests/shared_face_bodies_finish.rs` | - | 7 (6 ignored) |\n| Total | 6 (1 ignored) | 12 (6 ignored) |\n\n## Readings (release, `--ignored`, each band in its own process, all six at the same time)\n\nBefore: the old test `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_the_3d_finish` passed in 1804 s (30.1 min). It ran alone on this machine, from the `origin/main` source, after the band runs.\n\nAfter: the six band tests passed. Their sum is 527 s, and the slowest is 267 s:\n\n| Test | Wall time |\n|---|---|\n| `the_sample_as_imported_3d_finish_band_1_of_6_has_no_gouge` | 2 s |\n| `the_sample_as_imported_3d_finish_band_2_of_6_has_no_gouge` | 1 s |\n| `the_sample_as_imported_3d_finish_band_3_of_6_has_no_gouge` | 3 s |\n| `the_sample_as_imported_3d_finish_band_4_of_6_has_no_gouge` | 237 s |\n| `the_sample_as_imported_3d_finish_band_5_of_6_has_no_gouge` | 17 s |\n| `the_sample_as_imported_3d_finish_band_6_of_6_has_no_gouge` | 267 s |\n\nThe longest test is 4.5 min, under the 5 min limit of the issue. The bands are not equal: bands 4 and 6 hold most of the work. The wall time of the binary is the slowest band, about 4.5 min instead of 30 min.\n\nDebug, default suite: `shared_face_bodies` 5 passed (24.9 s); `shared_face_bodies_finish` 1 passed, 6 ignored (1.6 s). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test shared_face_bodies --test shared_face_bodies_finish -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Found on the way (issue #1840)\n\nThe job keeps the 3D Pocket R1, and the test never generates it. Thus `verify` skips its gate (`\"skipped\":\"an operation is stale or never generated - regenerate before judging the program\"`) and `gate.problems` is always empty. The no-gouge assert checked nothing in the old test, and it checks nothing in the band tests. This PR does not change the assert, because a split must not change an assert. Issue #1840 records this and the S1 shank/holder collision warnings that `verify` reports (the post is held by S1).\n\n## Overlap with open PRs #1772 and #1780\n\nThese PRs change the test `the_sample_as_imported_refuses_the_3d_pocket_by_name` and its doc comment in `shared_face_bodies.rs`. This PR does not touch that test or its comment. The removed lines end one unchanged blank line above their hunk. A trial merge (`git merge-tree`) of this branch with the current head of each PR gives one small conflict in `shared_face_bodies.rs`, because git sees the two hunks as adjacent. To resolve it, take the side of #1772 or #1780 and delete the old `the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_the_3d_finish` block (its doc comment, `#[test]`, `#[ignore]` and body) from it. No other file conflicts.\n\n## What was not run\n\n- The full quick gate. Only the two touched binaries and clippy on them ran.\n- The other heavy binaries of the release tier.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1715\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
